sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Daphnia magna ocellus-pigment Turing wavelength at 2.736 µm (Holocene, detail scale) — MorphoEval overall 84.0/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Schnakenberg reaction-diffusion on a periodic patch whose length unit puts the analytical critical wavelength at 2.736 µm (log10 = -5.563), the Holocene detail tier for Daphnia magna. The chronoseries is 1/1 at 0 Ma: there is no predecessor chronospecies and no successor. The solver's growth rates match σ(k) at Pearson r = 0.99999995 on the band around k_c (RMSE 0.00013). Raising D_u from 0.008 to 0.036 lengthens λ_c by a factor 2.21. Setting D_v = D_u drops the activator standard deviation to 0.286 of its initial value and the analytical max σ is negative. The CC BY-SA head SEM (Paulo Corgosinho, 2016) has a 100 µm bar measured at 156 px. Its cuticle mesh has an interior spectral peak at 20.17 µm, about seven times the model wavelength, so the polygons are not the Turing field. The saturated pattern's dominant wavelength is 3.72 µm, a nonlinear shift that Pass 1 does not yet treat as a held-out claim. The growth GIF has 12 frames at 720×540; its last frame is the SEM, which is the registration image for the fitness test. Overall 84.0/100 (faithfulness 82.7, reproducibility 87.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 86cc0374f85f7f6fea93d271291a5192c8f44eb3; environment: python 3.12, numpy 1.26.4, note scipy 1.18 and Pillow 13 installed for this run; no virtualenv. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/daphnia_magna_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 86cc0374f85f7f6fea93d271291a5192c8f44eb3, image/png, 343840 B, 1512×960 px, artifact_sha256 2ca968226229d47131b1597ba5722a3d2a086597c356cd8a4332a6c3e42ae30c (sha256 2ca968226229d47131b1597ba5722a3d2a086597c356cd8a4332a6c3e42ae30c), spec_fingerprint 5cc7a733d6eb0f2c8ca309d68942c0dd30e27b59c80a745c4958e462d76f9c31. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 5cc7a733d6eb0f2c8ca309d68942c0dd30e27b59c80a745c4958e462d76f9c31; artifact_sha256: 2ca968226229d47131b1597ba5722a3d2a086597c356cd8a4332a6c3e42ae30c. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a wavelength 2π/k_c from a dispersion relation. Schnakenberg (1979) supplies the kinetics du/dt = a − u + u²v, dv/dt = b − u²v. | Macagno (1981) showed that the Daphnia magna visual system is built by cellular interactions. Smith & Macagno (1990) resolved four spectral classes inside single ommatidia. Hebert & Emery (1990) showed that cuticular melanin is an inducible ultraviolet shield.; reconstructed_in_script: The length unit is chosen so λ_c = 2.736 µm. Parameters a = 0.062, b = 1.180, D_u = 0.016, D_v = 0.640 are not the slot-149 placeholders. | Nine Fourier modes are grown from the unstable eigenvector. Pearson r and RMSE compare those rates with σ(k) on the band σ > -0.15. A D_u sweep and an equal-diffusion ablation are included. | The SEM scale bar and an interior peak of the cuticle spectrum (20.17 µm) are measured on the vendored image.; transfer_boundary: The age delta along this chronoseries is zero. The comparison with a melanosome (~0.5 µm) and an ommatidium (tens of µm) is a scale comparison, not a fossil sequence. | Nothing here transfers to a claim that the ×130 cuticle polygons are a 2.736 µm pigment stripe.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a published measurement of a 2.736 µm ocellus stripe. That length is the assigned tier. | Does not claim the in-sample dispersion correlation is a held-out test. Odd modes are not yet withheld. | Does not claim a nanopublication signature. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is present. | Does not claim an independent second assessor scored this pass.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Hold out the odd-indexed Fourier modes and require Pearson r > 0.98 on that withheld set, not only on the full scored band.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Report the saturated wavelength divided by the analytical 2.736 µm as a coarsening ratio, so 3.72 µm is read as a nonlinear shift rather than a second target.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Nanopub signing is blocked: ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent. Do not invent a signature.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'State beside the circularity 0.018 that the perimeter follows the antennule and carapace folds, and keep the aspect ratio as the shape number.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.84"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single pass)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

